From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 14:41:20 -0400
Subject: spaces: sidebar backups, export and restore, in the importer's file
 format

SnapshotSidebar reads a window's sidebar into the Arc importer's plan
(Spaces with name, icon, colour and order; the essentials; per Space the
pinned run with its homes and the folders with their nesting; the loose
tabs; the user's tab names) and PlanToJson writes it in the shape
ParseArcSidebar reads, so an export is an import in reverse and a restore
applies through the importer: a merge that closes nothing, since a Space
named by its own id is that Space and a tab still open is skipped. Every
window writes a snapshot a minute after it opens and hourly after, into
the profile's "Sidebar Backups", kept as ten for today, one a day for ten
days, one a week for a month, one a month for a year. chrome://settings/
stedding lists the snapshots to restore, backs up now, exports the active
Space to Downloads and imports a sidebar file; the bar backs up and opens
the page (docs/features/import.md I17-I20).

Why: docs/ROUND6-PLAN.md wave 3, R6-29: PRODUCT's sidebar backups, and
the file-based answer to sync with no account.
Removable when: Chromium keeps versioned snapshots of its tab strip.
